WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.950
Hi everyone, it's Jerry. If you play the Ruy
Lopez or find yourself on the defending side

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:14.349
of it, the "Noah's Ark Trap" is something
for you to be aware of. It starts off after

00:00:14.349 --> 00:00:21.349
the moves e4, e5, knight f3, knight c6, bishop
b5, a6, and bishop a4. With now d6 we're entering

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:29.269
the Modern Steinitz variation of this opening.
Now a logical enough move for white is d4,

00:00:29.269 --> 00:00:33.230
striking in the center looking to maybe grab
on e, or even exploit the pin on the knight

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:39.370
with d5. But black has a good response. It's
b5 breaking the pin on the knight. And after

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:44.930
the bishop is kicked back, now a group of
three exchanges on d4. Starting first with

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:50.719
knight takes on d4, knight takes knight, e
takes knight. And if white is impatient, and

00:00:50.719 --> 00:00:56.579
immediately recaptures on d4, they've fallen
for the "Noah's Ark Trap". Now a better continuation

00:00:56.579 --> 00:01:00.890
at this point would be something like bishop
d5...the rook sidesteps the threat...we enter

00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:05.670
a roughly equal position. But just to highlight
what will happen if the queen immediately

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:11.220
recaptures on d4. We now have a flurry of
attacks and counterattacks, and after all

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:17.130
is said and done, it's black who gets the
last laugh. Here's how it works. It's c5 first,

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:22.670
striking at the queen, preparing c4 to trap
the bishop. And this can only be prevented

00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:28.950
for so long. After queen d5, an appealing
enough move. A duel threat hitting at f7 for

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:33.640
mate as well as the rook in the corner. There's
a convenient response however with bishop

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:38.369
e6, meeting everything...defending against
mate, defending the rook, and striking at

00:01:38.369 --> 00:01:43.009
the queen. After now queen c6, the bishop
retreats, but is still throwing a punch at

00:01:43.009 --> 00:01:48.710
the queen. After queen d5, we have now c4.
And this bishop is officially out of squares,

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:50.320
and the bishop is trapped.

